WEBVTT

00:00:01.945 --> 00:00:03.690
اَلْحَمْدُ لِلَّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينِ

00:00:03.714 --> 00:00:06.220
وَالصَّلاةُ وَالسَّلامُ عَلَى سَيِّدِ الْأَنْبِيَاءِ وَالْمُرْسَلِينِ

00:00:06.244 --> 00:00:11.200
وَعَلَى آلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ اَجْمَعِينَ  ثُمَّ اَمَّا بَعْدُ
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُم وَرَحْمَةُ اللهِ تَعَلَى وَ بَرَكَاتُهُ

00:00:11.224 --> 00:00:12.700
أَعُوذُ بِاللَّهِ مِنَ الشَّيطَانِ الرَّجِيمِ

00:00:12.724 --> 00:00:15.620
بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم
يس
وَالْقُرْآنِ الْحَكِيمِ

00:00:15.644 --> 00:00:16.961
إِنَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ

00:00:16.985 --> 00:00:19.540
عَلَى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيمٍ
تَنزِيلَ الْعَزِيزِ الرَّحِيمِ

00:00:19.564 --> 00:00:24.481
رَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِي صَدْرِي* وَيَسِّرْ لِي أَمْرِي* وَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِّن لِّسَانِي * يَفْقَهُوا قَوْلِي

00:00:24.545 --> 00:00:28.570
Surat Ya-Sin the opening of it, I'll read through it and give you the translation of it.

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:30.588
These are the first 12 Ayat of Surat Ya-Sin:

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.048
 يس وَالْقُرْآنِ الْحَكِيمِ 

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:36.280
I swear by the Qur'an full of wisdom and the one that is woven. Weaved together.

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:38.078
That's the meaning of the word Hakim (حكيم).

00:00:38.102 --> 00:00:39.390
إِنَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:41.860
Certainly you are truly from those that have been sent.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:45.493
عَلَى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيمٍ
on a straight path.

00:00:45.517 --> 00:00:47.150
تَنزِيلَ الْعَزِيزِ الرَّحِيمِ

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:50.570
A mighty revelation of the ultimate authority.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.540
The always Loving, Caring and Merciful. This is referring.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:56.740
This is describing the Qur'an that He's opened the swear-- the oath with.

00:00:56.764 --> 00:01:00.434
لِتُنذِرَ قَوْمًا مَّا أُنذِرَ آبَاؤُهُمْ
فَهُمْ غَافِلُونَ

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:05.010
The idea, in parenthesis, is this revelation has been sent for what purpose?

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.640
And why are you--why have you been sent?

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:10.710
So that you may warn a nation that was-- whose ancestors were not warned.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:12.460
And thus they are clueless.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:13.136
They're heedless.

00:01:13.184 --> 00:01:16.709
لَقَدْ حَقَّ الْقَوْلُ عَلَى
أَكْثَرِهِمْ فَهُمْ لا يُؤْمِنُونَ

00:01:16.733 --> 00:01:19.460
And certainly the truth
has manifested itself.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.060
The word has become abundantly clear to all of them.

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:25.739
Yet most of them are not going to believe.

00:01:25.764 --> 00:01:26.860
فَهُمْ لا يُؤْمِنُونَ

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:31.890
إِنَّا جَعَلْنَا فِي أَعْنَاقِهِمْ أَغْلالاً فَهِيَ إِلَى الأَذْقَانِ فَهُم مُّقْمَحُونَ

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:34.700
No doubt it is We that have placed, uh,

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:39.320
collars in their necks-- around their necks, all the way up to their chins.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:41.880
So they're strung up like this like there's a metal

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.210
collar in their neck and they can only look up.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.360
وَجَعَلْنَا مِن بَيْنِ أَيْدِيهِمْ سَدًّا
And We've placed a wall in front of them.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.650
وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ سَدًّا
And a wall behind them.

00:01:49.675 --> 00:01:51.760
فَأَغْشَيْنَاهُمْ
And We've covered them from above.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:52.945
فَهُمْ لاَ يُبْصِرُونَ

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:56.630
So they can only- their chained so they can only look up.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.300
But they can't see anything because it's covered.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:01:59.520
They can't see anything in front of them.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.500
They can't see anything behind them, so they're covered from all sides.

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.945
وَسَوَاء عَلَيْهِمْ أَأَنذَرْتَهُمْ أَمْ لَمْ تُنذِرْهُمْ لاَ يُؤْمِنُونَ

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:09.550
And it's the same for them whether you warn
them or not, they're not going to believe.

00:02:09.574 --> 00:02:15.080
إِنَّمَا تُنذِرُ مَنِ اتَّبَعَ الذِّكْرَ
You are only truly able to warn whoever would follow the reminder.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.750
وَخَشِيَ الرَّحْمَن بِالْغَيْبِ
And

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:22.650
would be fearful of the Incredibly Lovingly Merciful in the

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.260
unseen. Meaning when they are not seen by others

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.260
that's when they're fearful.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:29.416
Those are the only people
that will take heed of the warning.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:33.610
فَبَشِّرْهُ بِمَغْفِرَةٍ وَأَجْرٍ كَرِيمٍ
Then congratulate him,

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.760
such a person, of forgiveness and noble compensation.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.340
إِنَّا نَحْنُ نُحْيِي الْمَوْتَى
It is We, in fact,

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:40.833
that gives life to the dead.

00:02:40.857 --> 00:02:42.860
وَنَكْتُبُ مَا قَدَّمُوا وَآثَارَهُمْ

00:02:42.885 --> 00:02:45.020
And We document whatever they sent ahead.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:47.051
Whatever investments
they've made for their future.

00:02:47.075 --> 00:02:47.880
وَآثَارَهُمْ

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:51.080
and We also document whatever traces or consequences

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:53.250
they've left behind. The ruins in their wake.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:54.730
We document those as well.

00:02:54.755 --> 00:02:58.410
كُلَّ شَيْءٍ أَحْصَيْنَاهُ فِي إِمَامٍ مُبِينٍ
And all things

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:03.390
in fact, We have recorded thoroughly in an open, clear record. [إِمَامٍ مُبِينٍ]

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:06.700
There's a record with the possession of Allah in which all things are recorded.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.310
So this is briefly the passage.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.150
Now I've given some footnotes or some side notes here

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.420
to each group of Ayat or just single Ayat.

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:16.260
وَالْقُرْآنِ الْحَكِيمِ
إِنَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:19.087
عَلَى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيمٍ
تَنزِيلَ الْعَزِيزِ الرَّحِيمِ

00:03:19.112 --> 00:03:22.721
All of it dealing with revelation.
That clear everybody? Then I've said

00:03:22.745 --> 00:03:23.940
لِتُنذِرَ قَوْمًا

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:26.920
So that you may warn a nation whose ancestors were not warned.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:28.360
I said "so that you warn".

00:03:28.838 --> 00:03:30.971
لَقَدْ حَقَّ الْقَوْلُ عَلَى أَكْثَرِهِمْ

00:03:30.996 --> 00:03:34.260
Most of them won't believe, even though the truth has become clear to them.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:38.950
Then there's a middle: there there's the collar on their neck, the wall in front,

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:41.790
the wall behind, covered from all sides, blinded from all sides.

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:42.650
That's what I've said here.

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:46.155
Then the Allah says: Whether you
warn them or not, they won't believe.

00:03:46.187 --> 00:03:47.260
I wrote: They won't believe.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.980
Then you can only warn those who are truly are fearful.

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:54.920
So I said: Only warn the fearful. You can only warn the fearful.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.920
And finally, Allah has recorded everything in [ إِمَامٍ مُبِينٍ].

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:01.270
Now I'm going to color code this to illustrate some things to you.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:04.280
The opening section deals with revelation.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:07.000
The document that is in the possession of Allah: Allah's Word.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:11.150
And at the end, Allah Himself documents everything in the Book of Records.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:14.020
So there's two kinds of documents. That of revelation

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:15.730
and that that records all of our deeds.

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:18.240
And there's an interesting contrast between the two.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:20.130
One comes from the skies down to the earth.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:22.850
And the other is the document that's being produced here as

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:25.260
we do our deeds and then taken up for processing.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.820
The Book of Revelation that comes from the sky to

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:30.260
the earth is the one we're supposed to be judged

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:32.816
on the merits of and then Allah sees what

00:04:32.841 --> 00:04:35.470
changed in your behavior and that's recorded in this record.

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:39.260
So there are two divine records: one of revelation and one of our deeds.

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:41.630
And both of them are contrasted against each other

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.540
in the opening and closing of this passage. You'll notice Allah

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:45.870
secondly, talks about Inzar (انذار).

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:47.033
Which means to warn.

00:04:47.057 --> 00:04:51.110
لِتُنذِرَ قَوْمًا مَّا أُنذِرَ آبَاؤُهُمْ فَهُمْ غَافِلُونَ

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:53.252
That's the second passage-- second Ayah.

00:04:53.277 --> 00:04:55.890
And notice warning comes up again as the second last item.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.650
You can only warn those

00:04:58.640 --> 00:04:59.560
who are fearful.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:05.190
Allah is saying in the first one: Your job is to warn people that have been unaware,

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.730
and of these unaware there very few that in

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:09.700
their private moments are fearful of Allah.

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:11.770
Actually, you're only working on those.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:14.013
This is an important teaching for the Prophet ﷺ.

00:05:14.038 --> 00:05:17.440
On the one hand Allah has told him that most of them have no clue.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.230
Then He's told him:

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:22.440
And even the ones that do have a clue are going to be fearful of Allah, not publicly,

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:23.960
where they're going to be fearful of Allah?

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:25.940
[بِالْغَيْبِ] Privately.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:29.500
Which means even as you're reminding them and you see no reaction from them,

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:31.630
you keep teaching because you don't know what's

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:33.160
going to happen in their private moments.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:37.430
Don't let the visible lack of effect impact you and

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:40.320
take-- demoralize you that it's not having any impact.

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:40.860
Okay?

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.805
You find the third item Allah says is:

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:50.490
لَقَدْ حَقَّ الْقَوْلُ عَلَى أَكْثَرِهِمْ فَهُمْ لا يُؤْمِنُونَ
The truth has manifested itself,

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:52.250
and yet they won't believe.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:57.160
This is the idea that most of them, even though they know the truth, it won't matter.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:58.350
They're too stubborn.

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:04.530
And how stubborn are they that even if you were to warn them or not warn them,

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:06.930
they won't believe. Isn't that perfectly situated?

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:07.860
Right across.

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.660
Third last item?

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:13.260
I don't know why I didn't cover the whole line. It looks so nice anyway.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:17.280
And then right in the middle is the degree of their stubbornness.

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:19.150
How many ways are they covered in?

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:20.980
Three ways.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:22.890
They're looking up,

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:24.260
but the top is covered.

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:26.160
They can't move forward. What's there?

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:29.420
There's a wall in front. They can't see anything in front of them.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:31.290
And there's a wall behind them.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.238
Even though I'll be teaching you things about Surat Ya-Sin

00:06:33.263 --> 00:06:35.370
in the structure of Surahs section,

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:37.880
I will tell you one thing about the centrality of this Ayah.

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:40.110
This--these set of Ayat. This image that's been

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:42.140
painted of people that are blinded from above,

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:43.500
in front and behind.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:46.260
That's actually Allah's way of saying there are three ways of guidance.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:50.570
Guidance from above, guidance from the front and guidance from behind.

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:53.060
What does that mean? Guidance from above means revelation.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:56.740
Guidance from in front means look at the world in front of you.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:07:01.000
Look at the Ayat of Allah, ponder on them and you will find Allah. You'll find guidance.

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:02.860
What do you think behind refers to?

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:05.350
History. Very good.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:08.160
Look at history and you should learn learn something.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.730
You'll find as the Surah progresses

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:14.120
Allah will describe people who deny revelation. Allah will

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.360
describe people who deny history. Allah will

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:19.410
describe people who denied things that you can only learn from above.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:21.660
And then he denies--they denied the signs around them.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:25.190
The three kinds of blindness that are opening at the center of the

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:28.360
passage are going to be the primary subject matter of this Surah.

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:30.560
That's how the Surah is actually structured.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:33.270
It's giving you a clue as to what's coming into the Surah.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:36.050
Does everybody see the symmetrical structure in the opening passage?

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:43.000
Now this is beyond the (لطائف) and the (استنبات) you know (نكات بلاغية).

00:07:43.010 --> 00:07:46.560
It's like, you know, Farahi was saying: This is beyond just going to

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:49.660
discover cool beans in the Qur'an.

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:53.960
What's the purpose of this? A very important purpose of this is that you

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:58.860
appreciate which Ayat should be understood in light of which other Ayat.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:01.650
There's a progressive argument. We've studied that.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:04.420
But then there's another level of contemplation.

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:05.950
Once you understand this structure,

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:10.570
I should really compare and contrast this Ayah against this Ayah because they're

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:13.960
complimenting each other and they must go together to complete a lesson.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:17.310
They must have a purpose by which they are

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:19.890
now so directly related to each other literally.

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:23.160
فَهُمْ لا يُؤْمِنُونَ
لا يُؤْمِنُونَ

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:26.860
إِنَّمَا تُنذِرُ
لِتُنذِرَ

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.883
You know? Then here you have

00:08:29.907 --> 00:08:31.850
نَكْتُبُ
إِمَامٍ مُبِينٍ

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:33.570
And here you have
تَنزِيلَ الْعَزِيزِ الرَّحِيمِ

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:39.210
I mean, it's like very explicit correlations that are made. And remarkably

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:43.059
whatever Surahs I've studied so far in depth, I've found structures.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:46.820
That are just, they're all too obvious. They're very, very explicit.

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:51.020
But right now, we're still within the study of the structure of passages.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:54.330
Um, let me give you the next item, Inshallah. This one's clear?

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.350
Everybody, this case study is okay? Okay.

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:58.230
That would be the opening of Surat Ya-Sin.

00:08:58.254 --> 00:09:01.127
بِسْمِ اللَّهِ وَالصَّلاةُ وَالسَّلامُ عَلَى
رَسُولِ اللهِ وَعَلَى آلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ اَجْمَعِينَ

00:09:01.152 --> 00:09:03.260
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُم وَرَحْمَةُ اللهِ تَعَلَى وَ بَرَكَاتُهُ

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:04.660
This is

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:08.630
Ayahs number 40 to 122 of Surat al-Baqara.

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:10.550
We're not going to translate them.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:15.460
So this is I've grouped them together as a set of Ayat that

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:18.820
have one subject matter and these are the titles of those groups.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:20.350
The Ayah numbers are not relevant for this

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:22.520
discussion because there's just too many of them.

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:23.750
You won't be able to keep up anyway.

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:24.160
Okay?

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:27.710
So I'm just gonna read through this to show you how there are way too many

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:30.860
things going on. Just to give you an appreciation of how much is going on.

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:33.460
The first: Israelites be grateful and fearful.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.990
Then Allah talks about how they escaped from the Pharaoh.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:37.740
Then He talks about how they worshipped the calf.

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:40.470
You remember the calf story? The golden calf.

