Just like you know how we looked at the progression of an argument inside of a passage?

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:46.760
Now we're looking at the progression of an argument

00:21:47.140 --> 00:21:48.270
as an entire Surah.

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:51.280
Okay? So I'm gonna leave the discussion on Surah,

00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:55.580
what the definition of Surah is and the discourse about Surah for the next day.

00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:59.670
But for now, what I'm going to share with you is the coherence-- examples of some Surahs.

00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:01.860
And we'll start with our favorite Surah the Fatiha.

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:04.450
And highlight some things about the Fatiha.

00:22:05.140 --> 00:22:05.670
Now

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:09.770
I want to look at the first 3 Ayat of the Fatiha first.

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:12.220
الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ

00:22:12.490 --> 00:22:13.830
الرَّحْمَنِ الرَّحِيمِ

00:22:13.940 --> 00:22:14.950
مَالِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:18.690
I'm going to- for the purposes of discussing its linear coherence-

00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:20.770
take Fatiha 1 to 3.

00:22:24.740 --> 00:22:25.550
1 to 3.

00:22:25.940 --> 00:22:28.670
And I'm going to call them "knowledge".

00:22:33.940 --> 00:22:38.610
What do you learn in Fatiha 1 to 3. You learned that praise and gratitude belong to Allah.

00:22:38.610 --> 00:22:41.850
You learn some things about Allah. What knowledge do you acquire about Allah?

00:22:41.860 --> 00:22:46.000
That He is [رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ], [الرَّحْمَنِ الرَّحِيمِ] and, [مَالِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ].

00:22:46.290 --> 00:22:48.060
You learn these things about Allah.

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:51.220
When you get to [إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ]

00:22:51.550 --> 00:22:53.250
[وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ]

00:22:53.360 --> 00:22:54.670
That's Ayah number four.

00:22:55.140 --> 00:22:57.450
You are now in the realm of "action".

00:23:00.340 --> 00:23:01.960
What action are you ready to take now?

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:05.560
Engage in His worship.
[إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ]

00:23:06.040 --> 00:23:10.020
And you're ready to seek His help [وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ]. Now you're ready to take an action.

00:23:10.030 --> 00:23:15.460
So what the-- so far the linear progression is doing is: This knowledge of Allah

00:23:15.940 --> 00:23:18.060
should lead you to the following action.

00:23:18.940 --> 00:23:21.200
The knowledge of Allah, that is in [الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ]

00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:25.969
[الرَّحْمَنِ الرَّحِيمِ] [مَالِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ] leads to the act of

00:23:25.994 --> 00:23:28.770
[إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ] You with me so far?

00:23:29.340 --> 00:23:30.560
Okay? Now,

00:23:32.540 --> 00:23:35.170
of course, part of that action you can also say

00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:37.160
five

00:23:38.740 --> 00:23:39.670
we asked for what?

00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:42.860
We ask

00:23:43.840 --> 00:23:44.670
for

00:23:45.140 --> 00:23:48.898
guidance. Instead of spelling it out. Let me talk it out with you first.

00:23:48.923 --> 00:23:50.770
We asked for guidance along the

00:23:51.200 --> 00:23:54.570
straight path, which has been described as the path of those Allah

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:55.680
favored.

00:23:55.860 --> 00:23:57.640
Going on a path. Is that an action?

00:23:58.370 --> 00:24:03.300
And the people who went on that path did they go on that path with knowledge?

00:24:04.970 --> 00:24:06.270
That is the path

00:24:06.640 --> 00:24:07.660
of knowledge

00:24:08.540 --> 00:24:09.350
and action.

00:24:12.440 --> 00:24:16.312
People who knew
الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ. الرَّحْمَنِ الرَّحِيمِ. مَالِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ

00:24:16.337 --> 00:24:19.554
And as a result of that, they engaged in
إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ

00:24:19.579 --> 00:24:22.460
وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ
ended up on the straight path.

00:24:22.940 --> 00:24:27.170
We want to go on the path of those who learned that knowledge and applied that action

00:24:27.170 --> 00:24:29.450
and that's the summary of their life. Does that make sense to you?

00:24:30.040 --> 00:24:30.460
Okay?

00:24:30.940 --> 00:24:33.670
So that's what we're doing in Ayah number five

00:24:34.640 --> 00:24:39.670
and actually even six.
الصِّرَاطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ
صِرَاطَ الَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ

00:24:41.740 --> 00:24:43.270
Now, part of that

00:24:45.940 --> 00:24:48.060
is- what's coming next?

00:24:48.440 --> 00:24:49.960
غَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ

00:24:51.340 --> 00:24:52.270
Who are these people?

00:24:53.440 --> 00:24:54.760
You know how the Prophet described them?

00:24:56.140 --> 00:24:57.460
The people who earned anger?

00:24:57.840 --> 00:24:58.460
Who are they?

00:25:00.740 --> 00:25:01.960
Yeah.

00:25:02.740 --> 00:25:04.770
The Prophet would describe them as the Jews.

00:25:05.640 --> 00:25:09.170
But not all Jews. It's the Jews that are going to be talked about in Surat al-Baqara.

00:25:10.940 --> 00:25:15.990
It's going ahead. He's telling you this behavior. What-- Did the Jews know?

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:18.670
That the Qur'an keeps saying they have knowledge?

00:25:19.540 --> 00:25:22.423
يَتْلُونَ الْكِتَابَ
وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ
مِن بَعْدِ مَا عَقَلُوهُ

00:25:22.448 --> 00:25:23.660
After they understood it.

00:25:23.660 --> 00:25:26.770
They know the book. They recognize him like they recognize their own kids.

00:25:27.240 --> 00:25:28.260
Do they have knowledge?

00:25:28.940 --> 00:25:31.060
But did that knowledge translate into action?

00:25:32.240 --> 00:25:34.150
Not the path of

00:25:34.290 --> 00:25:36.170
knowledge without

00:25:36.940 --> 00:25:37.560
action.

00:25:39.740 --> 00:25:41.770
That's [الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ] Yes?

00:25:42.340 --> 00:25:47.456
And then what's the last wording?
الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلاَ الضَّالِّينَ

00:25:47.481 --> 00:25:50.950
[الضَّالِّينَ] are people that are lost.
When does somebody become lost?

00:25:50.950 --> 00:25:53.450
Lost means they're going on a road and that's the wrong road.

00:25:53.460 --> 00:25:55.060
Are they taking an act?

00:25:55.540 --> 00:25:57.270
They're engaged in an act of traveling.

00:25:57.280 --> 00:26:01.060
But they're going in the wrong direction because they have no what?

00:26:01.440 --> 00:26:04.950
Nor the path of action

00:26:05.740 --> 00:26:07.860
without knowledge.

00:26:09.940 --> 00:26:11.860
That's the linear progression of the Fatiha.

00:26:12.640 --> 00:26:13.960
It starts with knowledge.

00:26:14.540 --> 00:26:15.950
It progresses into action.

00:26:16.440 --> 00:26:17.780
Then you ask Allah, "Ya Allah,

00:26:17.780 --> 00:26:19.270
give me a life that is the balance

00:26:19.270 --> 00:26:22.790
between correct knowledge and correct action and save me

00:26:22.790 --> 00:26:25.420
from people that know but don't act. Or

00:26:25.420 --> 00:26:28.860
people that act and they unfortunately don't know."

00:26:30.540 --> 00:26:31.050
You see it?

00:26:33.940 --> 00:26:35.260
So that's not so hard to remember.

00:26:36.140 --> 00:26:36.560
Okay?

00:26:37.940 --> 00:26:39.770
Now my favorite,
Baqara. I can't help it.

00:26:41.840 --> 00:26:44.450
What course would be complete without linear coherence of Baqara?

00:26:46.540 --> 00:26:49.450
I'm going to give you the nine headings of Baqara.

00:26:55.940 --> 00:26:56.960
Faith

00:26:57.340 --> 00:26:58.360
disbelief

00:26:58.940 --> 00:27:00.260
and hypocrisy.

00:27:02.860 --> 00:27:03.770
That's a really big font.

00:27:05.340 --> 00:27:07.350
That's the first discussion in Baqara.

00:27:08.040 --> 00:27:09.960
Faith, disbelief and hypocrisy.

00:27:10.834 --> 00:27:13.117
هُدًى لِّلْمُتَّقِينَ
الَّذِينَ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْغَيْبِ

00:27:13.440 --> 00:27:14.550
إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ

00:27:14.813 --> 00:27:16.130
فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٌ

00:27:16.470 --> 00:27:17.060
Three groups.

00:27:18.740 --> 00:27:20.660
That transitions into the story of

00:27:21.240 --> 00:27:21.910
Adam 'alaihissalam.

00:27:22.540 --> 00:27:24.760
The story of Adam 'alaihissalam has faith.

00:27:25.740 --> 00:27:28.350
It has disbelief and it has hypocrisy.

00:27:29.735 --> 00:27:34.660
His disbelief came out and until then, until until the time that it had come out,

00:27:34.660 --> 00:27:35.950
what had it been all along?

00:27:36.640 --> 00:27:37.660
It had been hypocrisy.

00:27:38.440 --> 00:27:38.860
Okay?

00:27:39.440 --> 00:27:41.140
And I'm going to add something to it.

00:27:41.140 --> 00:27:43.440
You see how it progresses from the first discourse? This

00:27:43.660 --> 00:27:46.850
struggle between faith, disbelief and hypocrisy started with

00:27:47.240 --> 00:27:47.940
Adam 'alaihissalam.

00:27:48.300 --> 00:27:49.590
It's been going on since.

00:27:50.740 --> 00:27:53.670
And the story of Adam 'alaihissalam is the story of our father.

00:27:54.540 --> 00:27:56.670
Isn't it? So I'm just putting that as a side note.

00:27:57.240 --> 00:27:57.660
Okay?

00:27:59.940 --> 00:28:02.770
As soon as the story of Adam 'alaihissalam is done,

00:28:04.840 --> 00:28:06.080
you get Israelites.

00:28:06.640 --> 00:28:11.670
Actually, no. The Children of Israel. Uh, and they are children.

00:28:14.440 --> 00:28:15.670
Father followed by what?

00:28:16.340 --> 00:28:16.840
Children.

00:28:17.050 --> 00:28:18.110
Bani Israel.

00:28:19.540 --> 00:28:20.390
There's something else.

00:28:21.940 --> 00:28:23.610
Adam 'alaihissalam

00:28:23.780 --> 00:28:25.210
was tested.

00:28:26.540 --> 00:28:27.170
Was he?

00:28:29.540 --> 00:28:31.060
Were the Israelites tested?

00:28:31.840 --> 00:28:32.340
Yeah.

00:28:33.240 --> 00:28:36.770
Faith, belief and hypocrisy will only come out by way of what?

00:28:37.140 --> 00:28:37.990
Tests.

00:28:39.340 --> 00:28:41.100
And that started since Adam 'alaihissalam.

00:28:41.410 --> 00:28:42.960
Adam 'alaihissalam was tested.

00:28:43.340 --> 00:28:45.170
The Israelites are tested. Okay.

00:28:45.840 --> 00:28:49.290
As soon as the discussion of the Israelites is done, Allah

00:28:49.290 --> 00:28:52.050
talks about Ibrahim 'alaihissalam and he was also tested.

00:28:53.540 --> 00:28:54.320
Was he not?

00:28:54.345 --> 00:28:56.660
وَإِذِ ابْتَلَى إِبْرَاهِيمَ رَبُّهُ بِكَلِمَاتٍ

00:28:57.440 --> 00:29:00.460
So we've got-- And by the way, Ibrahim 'alaihissalam happens to be a

00:29:01.540 --> 00:29:02.270
father.

00:29:11.740 --> 00:29:14.170
Then we learn about the change of Qibla.

00:29:19.640 --> 00:29:20.560
From where to where?

00:29:27.440 --> 00:29:29.450
Interestingly, it's a it's a major test.

00:29:33.740 --> 00:29:36.050
That's where the testing comes to, uh, well,

00:29:36.940 --> 00:29:38.170
it gets more

00:29:38.840 --> 00:29:39.260
odd.

00:29:40.440 --> 00:29:42.860
Then we are made. We are new Ummah.

00:29:44.040 --> 00:29:46.365
وَكَذَلِكَ جَعَلْنَاكُمْ أُمَّةً وَسَطًا

00:29:46.390 --> 00:29:47.670
And our father is who?

00:29:48.740 --> 00:29:50.060
So we're Children of Ibrahim.

00:29:51.240 --> 00:29:52.187
And Allah says,

00:29:52.212 --> 00:29:55.170
وَلَنَبْلُوَنَّكُمْ بِشَيْءٍ مِّنَ الْخَوْفْ وَالْجُوعِ
We are going to be

00:29:55.640 --> 00:29:56.270
tested.

00:29:57.340 --> 00:29:57.960
Ya Allah.

00:30:00.840 --> 00:30:02.760
By the way, as far as children are-- Father,

00:30:03.140 --> 00:30:03.860
children,

00:30:04.340 --> 00:30:05.060
father,

00:30:05.440 --> 00:30:06.060
children.

00:30:07.040 --> 00:30:09.170
Which is--Qibla in the middle.

00:30:09.740 --> 00:30:10.270
Okay?

00:30:12.840 --> 00:30:16.560
Then there is a passage on the laws of Islam.

00:30:18.710 --> 00:30:25.660
These include laws of divorce, inheritance, diet, Hajj, fighting, fasting.

00:30:26.440 --> 00:30:26.950
You know?

00:30:27.340 --> 00:30:29.660
Multiple kinds of laws bunched together.

00:30:30.140 --> 00:30:31.060
Fifteen of them.

00:30:31.840 --> 00:30:32.260
Okay?

00:30:33.540 --> 00:30:36.170
Which are also a symmetrical like structure.

00:30:37.740 --> 00:30:39.770
They're completely symmetrical. You know what's in the middle?

00:30:40.340 --> 00:30:41.690
ادْخُلُواْ فِي السِّلْمِ كَافَّةً

00:30:42.740 --> 00:30:44.270
Come into Islam completely.

00:30:44.640 --> 00:30:45.450
It's amazing.

00:30:47.222 --> 00:30:48.160
Number eight.

00:30:48.940 --> 00:30:50.460
How many sections did I say they're going to be?

00:30:50.840 --> 00:30:51.460
Nine.

00:30:51.940 --> 00:30:52.940
Number eight

00:30:53.080 --> 00:30:55.080
is Islam's guidance on greed.

00:31:04.840 --> 00:31:06.760
Which is first spending

00:31:07.330 --> 00:31:08.050
then Riba

00:31:08.210 --> 00:31:09.060
then business.

00:31:14.340 --> 00:31:15.270
And finally,

00:31:15.740 --> 00:31:16.670
it's a prayer

00:31:18.540 --> 00:31:19.560
for help

00:31:20.540 --> 00:31:22.460
against tests.

00:31:30.840 --> 00:31:31.460
Okay.

00:31:32.240 --> 00:31:33.860
Now let me show you some progression.

00:31:35.840 --> 00:31:37.360
Adam 'alaihissalam was tested.

00:31:39.140 --> 00:31:39.670
With what?

00:31:42.040 --> 00:31:42.670
But what?

00:31:43.540 --> 00:31:44.350
With the tree.

00:31:45.240 --> 00:31:48.350
Was he able to succeed in that test? No.

00:31:48.510 --> 00:31:49.350
But

00:31:50.040 --> 00:31:52.460
what--After the after not succeeding

00:31:54.240 --> 00:31:55.260
didn't succeed

00:31:56.140 --> 00:31:57.160
but

00:31:57.840 --> 00:31:58.460
repented.

00:31:59.140 --> 00:31:59.670
Yes?

00:32:00.840 --> 00:32:03.270
The Children of Israelites were tested. Yes or no?

00:32:04.440 --> 00:32:05.360
Did they succeed?

00:32:07.140 --> 00:32:08.270
Didn't succeed.

00:32:09.540 --> 00:32:10.560
Didn't repent.

00:32:12.240 --> 00:32:14.460
Ibrahim 'alaihissalam was tested. Yes or no?

00:32:15.340 --> 00:32:16.380
Succeeded or no?

00:32:16.670 --> 00:32:18.230
[فَأَتَمَّهُنَّ] succeeded.

00:32:18.360 --> 00:32:19.560
And still repented.

00:32:24.540 --> 00:32:27.815
So he says,
وَتُبْ عَلَيْنَا إِنَّكَ أَنتَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ

00:32:27.840 --> 00:32:29.550
So do you only repent when you fail?

00:32:30.640 --> 00:32:32.860
You're supposed to repent anyway. Part of your success is repenting.

00:32:33.640 --> 00:32:34.060
Okay?

00:32:35.740 --> 00:32:39.960
Change of Qibla happens. We'll skip that. The new Ummah is tested.

00:32:41.540 --> 00:32:42.757
And there is a:

00:32:43.340 --> 00:32:45.950
will you succeed? Will you fail? And will you repent?

00:32:47.240 --> 00:32:49.360
There are three case studies before you.

00:32:49.940 --> 00:32:51.260
What are the three case studies?

00:32:51.640 --> 00:32:55.720
The way of Adam. You might fail at some point. You might not succeed.

00:32:55.730 --> 00:32:58.960
But when you don't succeed, what should you do? Repent.

00:32:58.970 --> 00:33:02.670
You can also very well go down the road of the Israelites. And what's going to happen?

00:33:03.640 --> 00:33:05.690
You're going to become the cursed nation. Because

00:33:05.690 --> 00:33:08.340
they didn't succeed and they didn't repent.

00:33:08.350 --> 00:33:10.200
But you are the children of your father

00:33:10.200 --> 00:33:15.360
so I have full expectation that you will do what things? Succeed and also repent.

00:33:16.240 --> 00:33:17.350
You will succeed and you wil repent.

00:33:17.740 --> 00:33:20.870
Do you see a progression? But before we get to

00:33:20.870 --> 00:33:23.950
us, what was placed deliberately in between us and Ibrahim?

00:33:26.940 --> 00:33:30.910
Because you need to remember that you are the legacy of your father, Ibrahim.

00:33:30.910 --> 00:33:35.884
And nothing will remind you better that you are associated with Ibrahim than what?

00:33:35.908 --> 00:33:36.947
The Qibla.

00:33:37.344 --> 00:33:38.209
The Qibla.

00:33:39.040 --> 00:33:43.960
So before you're inaugurated as the as the children of your father, Ibrahim,

00:33:44.440 --> 00:33:47.670
you must first commemorate the House that was built by him.

00:33:48.340 --> 00:33:48.670
Okay?

00:33:50.940 --> 00:33:52.860
You're going to be tested with what?

00:33:53.440 --> 00:33:54.160
Exactly.

00:33:55.040 --> 00:33:57.010
Well, the nation before you was tested with laws.

00:33:58.040 --> 00:34:00.050
Your test is coming, and it's going to be with what?

00:34:01.240 --> 00:34:03.760
So there's a bunch of laws of Islam.

00:34:04.840 --> 00:34:06.270
Which will put you to the test.

00:34:07.140 --> 00:34:09.630
You're being tested, whether or not you uphold the Law.

00:34:09.699 --> 00:34:11.060
Like which nation before you?

00:34:11.840 --> 00:34:13.360
The Israelites. Okay.

00:34:15.739 --> 00:34:17.260
Of all of the laws,

00:34:17.260 --> 00:34:19.199
there seems to be one matter that will be

00:34:19.199 --> 00:34:21.219
the hardest test for you more than anything else.

00:34:22.840 --> 00:34:23.469
What is that?

00:34:25.139 --> 00:34:25.760
Greed.

00:34:27.739 --> 00:34:28.670
Green is gonna get you.

00:34:29.540 --> 00:34:32.199
So though all the laws were described in brief,

00:34:32.460 --> 00:34:34.159
which law is exhaustive?

00:34:35.340 --> 00:34:35.760
Greed.

00:34:36.639 --> 00:34:38.560
By the way that takes us back to Adam 'alaihissalam.

00:34:39.540 --> 00:34:43.219
Adam 'alaihissalam's test was actually one of greed. You have all the trees

00:34:43.219 --> 00:34:44.760
in Jannah, just stay away from this one.

00:34:46.340 --> 00:34:46.670
Right?

00:34:47.040 --> 00:34:50.419
It's no accident that when Allah gives us the guidance on greed, He says:

00:34:50.444 --> 00:34:52.580
الشَّيْطَانُ يَعِدُكُمُ الْفَقْرَ

00:34:52.750 --> 00:34:54.170
Shaytan is gonna promise bankruptcy to you.

00:34:55.520 --> 00:34:59.460
In between the lines Shaytan will promise you bankruptcy just like he promised who?

00:35:00.840 --> 00:35:01.670
Adam 'alaihissalam.

00:35:02.740 --> 00:35:04.260
Do you see a progression?

00:35:05.040 --> 00:35:06.950
When you get to the guidance on greed

00:35:06.950 --> 00:35:09.590
Allah says: Here is the best thing you can do to fight greed.

00:35:09.600 --> 00:35:11.550
Here is the best thing you can do with your money,

00:35:11.550 --> 00:35:13.860
which is what? Spend in the path of Allah.

00:35:15.140 --> 00:35:16.360
Spend in the path of Allah.

00:35:17.840 --> 00:35:19.670
And what's the worst thing you can do with your money?

00:35:20.740 --> 00:35:21.250
Riba.

00:35:21.740 --> 00:35:24.470
And what's the acceptable thing you can do with your money?

00:35:24.840 --> 00:35:25.500
Business.

00:35:25.940 --> 00:35:28.550
One extreme, then the other extreme, then the middle.

00:35:29.840 --> 00:35:32.640
And now that you've been given all that you need to be given,

00:35:32.640 --> 00:35:34.210
here's what you're going to be tested with.

00:35:34.210 --> 00:35:38.560
This is your trial as an Ummah. Now you turn back to Allah and you say

00:35:39.015 --> 00:35:42.668
اَ تَحْمِلْ عَلَيْنَا إِصْرًا كَمَا حَمَلْتَهُ عَلَى الَّذِينَ مِن قَبْلِنَا

00:35:42.693 --> 00:35:46.360
Master, don't put a burden on us like You put on those who came before us,

00:35:46.840 --> 00:35:48.460
that we don't have the power to bear.

00:35:49.240 --> 00:35:55.018
وَانصُرْنَا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكَافِرِينَ
وَاعْفُ عَنَّا وَاغْفِرْ لَنَا وَارْحَمْنَا أَنتَ مَوْلانَا فَانصُرْنَا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكَافِرِينَ

00:35:55.042 --> 00:35:57.042
Pardon us, cover for us

00:35:57.840 --> 00:36:01.050
You are our guardian. You are our protector. Aid us against disbelieving people.

00:36:01.930 --> 00:36:03.250
This is the progressive,

00:36:03.630 --> 00:36:05.140
discourse of Baqara.

00:36:05.140 --> 00:36:09.050
And since we're on it and I kind of shared it with you anyway, look at the symmetry.

00:36:10.230 --> 00:36:12.540
Faith, belief and hypocrisy.

00:36:13.330 --> 00:36:17.780
And the last Du'a is actually about faith, belief and hypocrisy--Faith,

00:36:17.780 --> 00:36:19.070
disbelief and hypocrisy.

00:36:19.080 --> 00:36:22.660
It's about faith
آمَنَ الرَّسُولُ بِمَا أُنزِلَ إِلَيْهِ مِن رَّبِّهِ وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ

00:36:24.030 --> 00:36:27.650
It's about hypocrisy: Don't make us not carry the burden

00:36:27.650 --> 00:36:29.550
like the the Israelites were not able to carry

00:36:29.550 --> 00:36:32.470
their burden and became hypocrites. And keep us from

00:36:32.470 --> 00:36:35.744
the disbelievers
فَانصُرْنَا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكَافِرِينَ

00:36:35.769 --> 00:36:38.850
The story Adam 'alaihissalam is actually a story of greed.

00:36:41.330 --> 00:36:45.250
The Children of Israel messed up their laws. You better not mess up

00:36:45.630 --> 00:36:46.530
your laws.

00:36:46.840 --> 00:36:49.510
Ibrahim 'alaihissalam was tested and succeeded.

00:36:49.640 --> 00:36:51.150
Now you're going to be tested.

00:36:53.230 --> 00:36:55.660
And in the middle of it is the middle of this Ummah, the Qibla.

00:36:56.930 --> 00:36:59.210
Where everything switches and the Qibla also is

00:36:59.210 --> 00:37:01.610
a switch from the Israelites to the Muslims.

00:37:01.620 --> 00:37:05.800
Just like the first half is working up towards the end of the Israelites.

00:37:05.810 --> 00:37:08.180
And the second half is turning towards the Ummah.

00:37:08.190 --> 00:37:11.450
The Qibla itself is the point at which everything turns.

00:37:13.330 --> 00:37:16.750
So the whole thing converges at the change of the Qibla.

00:37:18.130 --> 00:37:18.550
Okay?

00:37:19.130 --> 00:37:21.650
That's a little bit about Baqara, and it's linear coherence.

00:37:22.530 --> 00:37:23.140
Um,

00:37:23.150 --> 00:37:27.750
I'm gonna try to knock out the- a brief overview of the

00:37:27.750 --> 00:37:30.960
coherence of Surat al-Kahf before I let you guys go today.

00:37:30.970 --> 00:37:31.650
That okay with you?

00:37:32.130 --> 00:37:36.150
Okay. Even if it's not, it's your problem. Okay.

00:37:36.830 --> 00:37:37.660
Surat al-Kahf.

00:37:38.030 --> 00:37:39.350
Ayahs number 1 to 8.

00:37:46.430 --> 00:37:47.240
The book

00:37:48.370 --> 00:37:49.650
stands firm

00:37:50.930 --> 00:37:53.840
to warn against great trials.

00:37:56.330 --> 00:38:00.950
That's the theme of one to eight.
قَيِّمًا لِّيُنذِرَ بَأْسًا شَدِيدًا مِن لَّدُنْهُ

00:38:02.320 --> 00:38:04.330
Ayahs number 9 to 26

00:38:04.920 --> 00:38:06.330
are the youth of the cave.

00:38:09.020 --> 00:38:12.040
Is there a correlation between great trials and the youth of the cave?

00:38:13.520 --> 00:38:16.490
The youth of the cave are barely able to hold onto their faith.

00:38:16.500 --> 00:38:20.330
First of all, from external pressures, they might be executed. They will be killed.

00:38:20.340 --> 00:38:21.340
They're running into a cave.

00:38:21.340 --> 00:38:23.750
Second of all they're young people; young people want to live their life.

00:38:23.750 --> 00:38:25.040
They want to enjoy themselves.

00:38:25.420 --> 00:38:27.730
And they're fighting against their inner Nafs and

00:38:27.730 --> 00:38:29.500
the outer forces and holding onto the Iman.

00:38:29.500 --> 00:38:30.540
What bigger trial than that?

00:38:31.820 --> 00:38:33.260
And Allah 'azzawajal aided them

00:38:33.285 --> 00:38:36.040
and He's aiding you with something much more powerful; the Qur'an itself.

00:38:36.720 --> 00:38:37.140
Then

00:38:38.020 --> 00:38:40.280
27 to 31

00:38:40.590 --> 00:38:41.830
the Prophet is told:

00:38:42.920 --> 00:38:45.740
Stand by the weak companions

00:38:49.420 --> 00:38:50.920
as they are

00:38:51.030 --> 00:38:52.240
with Allah.

00:38:53.920 --> 00:38:56.760
Don't be impressed with the leaders. Don't be impressed with the elite.

00:38:56.760 --> 00:38:59.180
They're not your support, the weak companions are your support.

00:38:59.190 --> 00:39:03.040
Is there a correlation between the youth of the cave and standing by the weak?

00:39:03.520 --> 00:39:05.140
Do you see it, or do I have to spell it out?

00:39:05.820 --> 00:39:08.580
It's obvious, yes? They were powerless

00:39:08.580 --> 00:39:10.850
young people and the Sahaba around you are powerless

00:39:10.850 --> 00:39:13.950
and yet they are powerful to Allah because they're connected with Allah 'azzawajal.

00:39:14.420 --> 00:39:14.840
Okay?

00:39:15.520 --> 00:39:19.222
And by the way, in that passage, 27 to 31 always has things like

00:39:19.247 --> 00:39:23.040
وَقُلِ الْحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّكُمْ
Say, the truth comes from your Master. What does that echo?

00:39:23.050 --> 00:39:27.940
It echoes how the youth of the cave stood up and said:
رَبُّنَا رَبُّ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالأَرْضِ

00:39:28.620 --> 00:39:30.150
Didn't they come up and get up and say that?

00:39:30.520 --> 00:39:33.670
Similarly, these Ayat say, you know those who do good deeds

00:39:33.670 --> 00:39:36.540
they believe and do good deeds
إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ

00:39:37.920 --> 00:39:40.140
About these people
إِنَّا لا نُضِيعُ أَجْرَ مَنْ أَحْسَنَ عَمَلا

00:39:41.020 --> 00:39:43.530
We're not gonna waste their deeds. What--

00:39:43.530 --> 00:39:46.230
What is Allah saying? People of wealth and power

00:39:46.240 --> 00:39:47.730
everything they have is going to go to waste.

00:39:47.730 --> 00:39:50.230
The only thing that won't go to waste, the most valuable

00:39:50.230 --> 00:39:52.950
treasure is people that are committed to faith and doing right.

00:39:53.420 --> 00:39:55.560
Those are the most valuable assets. Okay?

00:39:55.570 --> 00:39:57.588
And they may not have worldly treasure, but

00:39:57.613 --> 00:39:58.840
أُوْلَئِكَ لَهُمْ جَنَّاتُ

00:39:59.220 --> 00:40:01.440
They're going to have gardens. Okay?

00:40:01.910 --> 00:40:02.440
Now

00:40:03.110 --> 00:40:04.430
speaking of gardens.

00:40:05.510 --> 00:40:08.830
Ayah 32 to 44 is this story

00:40:09.070 --> 00:40:09.640
of

00:40:10.010 --> 00:40:10.820
the gardener.

00:40:13.410 --> 00:40:14.640
Gardener.

00:40:15.410 --> 00:40:16.430
And his neighbor.

00:40:17.410 --> 00:40:18.240
You know this story?

00:40:19.710 --> 00:40:23.330
Vie for the right kind of garden and don't get lost in the wrong kind of garden.

00:40:25.410 --> 00:40:28.440
And so thus comes the story of the gardener's trial.

00:40:29.310 --> 00:40:29.820
Then

00:40:31.110 --> 00:40:33.240
45 to 59.

00:40:35.210 --> 00:40:37.640
Allah basically teaches: Nothing in life is permanent.

00:40:40.255 --> 00:40:44.840
وَاضْرِبْ لَهُم مَّثَلَ الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا كَمَاء أَنزَلْنَاهُ مِنَ السَّمَاء فَاخْتَلَطَ بِهِ نَبَاتُ الأَرْضِ

00:40:44.864 --> 00:40:49.377
فَأَصْبَحَ هَشِيمًا تَذْرُوهُ الرِّيَاحُ وَكَانَ اللَّهُ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ مُّقْتَدِرًا

00:40:49.401 --> 00:40:52.700
الْمَالُ وَالْبَنُونَ زِينَةُ الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا

00:40:53.210 --> 00:40:58.330
Worldly life is like a plant that grew then dried up and its leaves are crushed away.

00:40:58.330 --> 00:41:00.830
Nothing is permanent. Is that connected to the gardener story?

00:41:01.710 --> 00:41:03.740
He had so much and it wasn't permanent.

00:41:04.410 --> 00:41:05.080
Then, He says

00:41:05.080 --> 00:41:09.240
the only thing that will matter is you're going to come in front of Us alone.

00:41:09.250 --> 00:41:11.130
كَمَا خَلَقْنَاكُمْ أَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ

00:41:11.155 --> 00:41:13.440
لَّقَدْ جِئْتُمُونَا كَمَا خَلَقْنَاكُمْ أَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ

00:41:14.210 --> 00:41:16.640
Nothing in life is permanent except

00:41:17.310 --> 00:41:18.330
your deeds

00:41:19.010 --> 00:41:20.740
and the afterlife.

00:41:21.410 --> 00:41:21.640
Okay?

00:41:23.610 --> 00:41:24.830
That's the theme here.

00:41:25.810 --> 00:41:27.130
Everything else will disappear.

00:41:29.610 --> 00:41:30.140
Then

00:41:32.610 --> 00:41:33.830
62

00:41:34.310 --> 00:41:35.240
82.

00:41:37.710 --> 00:41:40.020
Musa 'alaihissalam's

00:41:41.510 --> 00:41:42.640
three-part journey.

00:41:50.610 --> 00:41:51.630
What could be the connection?

00:41:53.510 --> 00:41:54.830
Nothing in life is permanent.

00:41:55.510 --> 00:41:57.900
What is life all together? Where did this Surah begin?

00:41:58.110 --> 00:42:02.972
It began within
إِنَّا جَعَلْنَا مَا عَلَى الأَرْضِ زِينَةً لَّهَا لِنَبْلُوَهُمْ

00:42:03.016 --> 00:42:05.660
Sometimes the tests of life are really, really hard.

00:42:06.200 --> 00:42:07.820
We forget why we're really here.

00:42:08.200 --> 00:42:10.320
This life can become so taxing that we forget

00:42:10.320 --> 00:42:12.610
there's something- there's a larger plan.

00:42:13.000 --> 00:42:16.230
Musa 'alaihissalam is going to see things happen in worldly life that he can't tolerate.

00:42:17.800 --> 00:42:19.890
Even though it's temporary in front of him.

00:42:19.890 --> 00:42:23.910
And Allah has a plan not only for material reasons like the gardener,

00:42:23.920 --> 00:42:26.410
even for faith reasons, you can become this--

00:42:26.420 --> 00:42:28.930
or you can become concerned about worldly matters.

00:42:29.400 --> 00:42:30.840
And overindulge in them.

00:42:30.990 --> 00:42:33.230
Musa 'alaihissalam is going to learn some very difficult lessons.

00:42:33.230 --> 00:42:34.730
Can you tell me what the three stops were?

00:42:37.400 --> 00:42:39.110
Good. Ship.

00:42:40.100 --> 00:42:41.200
The boy.

00:42:41.500 --> 00:42:42.010
The wall.

00:42:42.270 --> 00:42:42.730
Okay.

00:42:43.900 --> 00:42:45.010
You guys are amazing.

00:42:45.400 --> 00:42:47.430
83 to 99.

00:42:49.000 --> 00:42:49.810
Zul Qarnain.

00:42:53.400 --> 00:42:54.630
And his three stops.

00:42:57.100 --> 00:42:58.230
Does he also have three stops?

00:42:58.900 --> 00:43:00.430
Yep. He does.

00:43:01.000 --> 00:43:02.710
What are his three stops?

00:43:04.100 --> 00:43:06.020
Well, we don't really know. Jersey?

00:43:14.507 --> 00:43:16.730
Right? So he heads west

00:43:17.300 --> 00:43:18.530
and he does

00:43:18.700 --> 00:43:19.950
west to do justice,

00:43:23.000 --> 00:43:23.520
right?

00:43:23.730 --> 00:43:25.120
Then he goes east

00:43:25.500 --> 00:43:27.020
and leaves alone.

00:43:27.400 --> 00:43:30.229
He meets people that are under the "no shade".

00:43:30.254 --> 00:43:33.930
[كذلك تركناهه يعني كذلك تركناهم كذلك]
He left them be.

00:43:34.700 --> 00:43:37.010
And then he went to Ya'juj and Ma'juj.

00:43:38.000 --> 00:43:38.420
Right?

00:43:39.000 --> 00:43:40.620
And he built a wall.

00:43:42.400 --> 00:43:45.010
I put that there on purpose. What was the third item in the story of Musa?

00:43:46.100 --> 00:43:47.020
Yep. Wall; wall.

00:43:48.200 --> 00:43:49.310
Okay, we'll come back to that.

00:43:51.000 --> 00:43:52.020
Well, no, I'll tell you now.

00:43:53.600 --> 00:43:59.450
The story of Musa 'alaihissalam begins with an attempt to, uh, no, I can't start.

00:43:59.460 --> 00:44:00.800
No, no, no. I'll wait.

00:44:03.190 --> 00:44:03.910
100

00:44:04.290 --> 00:44:05.010
to 110.

00:44:10.090 --> 00:44:11.410
The real punishment.

00:44:15.390 --> 00:44:16.610
And real reward.

00:44:18.990 --> 00:44:20.910
Meaning the real punishment for bad people

00:44:22.190 --> 00:44:23.300
and real reward

00:44:23.690 --> 00:44:24.610
for good people

00:44:27.090 --> 00:44:28.800
is in the afterlife.

00:44:30.990 --> 00:44:34.920
And also Allah says: If the Words of Allah

00:44:38.990 --> 00:44:40.310
are an endless what?

00:44:41.590 --> 00:44:42.100
Ocean.

00:44:43.790 --> 00:44:44.210
Okay?

00:44:45.590 --> 00:44:47.630
Which, by the way, picks up on the last two stories.

00:44:47.640 --> 00:44:50.570
He goes to where the sun sets in water. He's heading towards water.

00:44:50.570 --> 00:44:53.260
Musa 'alaihissalam goes to the place where the oceans meet and Allah

00:44:53.260 --> 00:44:55.450
is now saying the Words of Allah are an endless ocean.

00:44:56.790 --> 00:45:00.470
Okay, anyway, now let's understand the the,

00:45:00.480 --> 00:45:02.720
uh progression at a little bit of a deeper level.

00:45:03.390 --> 00:45:05.310
Basically, what you find in Surat al-Kahf

00:45:05.690 --> 00:45:06.320
is

00:45:06.620 --> 00:45:09.610
what you can call sermon-story, sermon-story.

00:45:10.190 --> 00:45:11.720
So 1 to 8 is sermon.

00:45:17.290 --> 00:45:18.310
Followed by a story.

00:45:19.590 --> 00:45:21.920
Followed by another sermon; 27 to 31.

00:45:23.390 --> 00:45:24.410
Followed by a story

00:45:24.790 --> 00:45:26.410
followed by another sermon where

00:45:27.490 --> 00:45:28.810
45 to 59.

00:45:29.490 --> 00:45:30.640
Followed by a story.

00:45:31.390 --> 00:45:33.980
And then followed by another story; two stories in a row.

00:45:33.990 --> 00:45:38.010
Which leaves one more sermon 110, 100 to 110.

00:45:42.490 --> 00:45:44.140
The thing to understand is

00:45:44.790 --> 00:45:46.090
the first sermon

00:45:46.380 --> 00:45:47.720
leads into the

00:45:48.390 --> 00:45:48.920
story.

00:45:49.790 --> 00:45:53.820
That story leads into the next sermon, which leads into the next story.

00:45:53.830 --> 00:45:57.110
Each one of them are actually pushing you into the next and to the next.

00:45:57.590 --> 00:45:59.180
For the purposes of brevity

00:45:59.210 --> 00:46:02.250
I'm only going to highlight matters that pertain to the stories.

00:46:02.780 --> 00:46:04.380
And I'll teach you something about how the

00:46:04.380 --> 00:46:06.710
stories are part of a progressive argument.

00:46:07.280 --> 00:46:11.890
Okay? The four stories of the Surah are connected. Some have made the connection

00:46:11.900 --> 00:46:15.710
there are four kinds of trials. The trial of youth,

00:46:16.280 --> 00:46:17.710
the trial of wealth,

00:46:18.280 --> 00:46:19.820
the trial of knowledge

00:46:20.070 --> 00:46:21.210
and the trial of power.

00:46:22.180 --> 00:46:25.620
Right? That's how some have described the four trials are connected.

00:46:25.630 --> 00:46:28.010
I would take a different approach even though I find

00:46:28.010 --> 00:46:29.960
some benefit in that; I'm taking a different approach.

00:46:29.960 --> 00:46:31.000
So let me explain that to you.

00:46:31.680 --> 00:46:36.700
The Surah is essentially a call for believing in the

00:46:36.710 --> 00:46:39.800
unseen and letting go of what you see materially.

00:46:40.980 --> 00:46:44.200
The primary objective of the Surah is to

00:46:44.200 --> 00:46:46.640
get you to really internalize that there's the

00:46:46.640 --> 00:46:50.400
reality that you cannot see is more powerful than the reality that you can see.

00:46:51.180 --> 00:46:51.380
Okay?

00:46:51.380 --> 00:46:55.710
The unseen is a more powerful reality than the physical laws of

00:46:55.710 --> 00:46:57.800
nature and the things you have in front of your eyes.

00:46:57.810 --> 00:46:58.500
Okay?

00:46:59.480 --> 00:47:01.630
And you have to believe that in that unseen

00:47:01.630 --> 00:47:04.970
reality- in the seen reality physics is at work,

00:47:04.980 --> 00:47:10.600
gravity is at work, chemistry is at work, biology is at work. In the unseen reality

00:47:10.610 --> 00:47:12.100
Allah is at work constantly.

00:47:12.880 --> 00:47:14.850
Allah is the driver over all things

00:47:14.970 --> 00:47:17.800
that you see. And more importantly, stuff you don't see

00:47:18.280 --> 00:47:20.910
Things that are not, you know, visible to your eyes. Now

00:47:21.480 --> 00:47:24.800
if you then look at it from that point of view. What's the first story?

00:47:26.280 --> 00:47:27.300
Youth of the Cave.

00:47:27.880 --> 00:47:31.450
And the youth of the cave, Allah--There's divine intervention.

00:47:35.380 --> 00:47:36.790
And there is apparent relief.

00:47:39.680 --> 00:47:41.410
What's the Divine intervention in this story?

00:47:43.980 --> 00:47:47.100
They were able to sleep more than scientifically possible.

00:47:47.880 --> 00:47:48.300
Right?

00:47:49.580 --> 00:47:53.000
That intervention--Is the intervention of Allah invisible

00:47:53.000 --> 00:47:54.290
or did it become visible now?

00:47:55.180 --> 00:47:56.110
It became visible.

00:47:56.780 --> 00:47:57.290
And

00:47:57.780 --> 00:48:00.290
so did the relief that came from the intervention of Allah.

00:48:01.270 --> 00:48:04.690
If you compare this to the story of the gardeners, what happened to his garden?

00:48:06.770 --> 00:48:10.790
How was it destroyed, did somebody like set it on fire?

00:48:12.770 --> 00:48:16.400
It was a storm. And a storm can only come from?

00:48:17.670 --> 00:48:18.990
Divine intervention, clearly.

00:48:22.870 --> 00:48:25.000
And apparently was their relief?

00:48:27.570 --> 00:48:28.790
Apparently, there's a stress.

00:48:30.170 --> 00:48:32.290
His garden is destroyed, he's distressful, isn't he?

00:48:33.340 --> 00:48:36.780
But in both of these cases, is the intervention from Allah visible?

00:48:37.770 --> 00:48:38.280
Yes.

00:48:38.970 --> 00:48:41.400
I mean, the storm only came from Allah, no human being did it

00:48:42.770 --> 00:48:43.190
Now

00:48:44.070 --> 00:48:45.000
come to Musa's story?

00:48:47.370 --> 00:48:49.200
The ship is cracked by who?

00:48:51.370 --> 00:48:51.900
Khidr.

00:48:52.370 --> 00:48:53.390
The boy is killed by who?

00:48:54.220 --> 00:48:55.000
Khidr.

00:48:55.770 --> 00:48:58.249
The ship--The wall is built by who?
Khidr and Musa.

00:48:59.870 --> 00:49:01.700
Looks like it's human intervention,

00:49:04.270 --> 00:49:04.590
right?

00:49:07.070 --> 00:49:08.640
And apparently there's distress.

00:49:13.570 --> 00:49:15.726
Actually, I won't even
call it human intervention.

00:49:15.751 --> 00:49:20.780
I'm gonna say "not
visible divine intervention".

00:49:22.370 --> 00:49:26.390
By the end of the story, what does Khidr say? This was all by the decree of

00:49:27.270 --> 00:49:30.460
مَا فَعَلْتُهُ عَنْ أَمْرِي
I didn't do this on my own.

00:49:30.620 --> 00:49:31.790
This was divine intervention.

00:49:32.170 --> 00:49:34.390
But it wasn't-- It looked like it was Khidr doing it.

00:49:34.970 --> 00:49:35.780
Every time.

00:49:36.170 --> 00:49:36.700
Okay.

00:49:37.770 --> 00:49:39.113
Then you get to Zul Qarnain's story.

00:49:39.138 --> 00:49:40.790
What's he doing wherever he goes?

00:49:43.370 --> 00:49:47.900
He's fixing a problem, or he's leaving them alone. Or he's building a massive wall.

00:49:49.170 --> 00:49:51.390
Looks like who's intervening, Allah or Zul Qarnain?

00:49:51.970 --> 00:49:54.310
So it's "not visible divine intervention".

00:49:57.770 --> 00:49:59.390
And there's apparent, what?

00:50:00.860 --> 00:50:04.780
Distress or relief? You see the possibilities that have been opened up?

00:50:05.660 --> 00:50:08.310
Allah's intervention is sometimes visible, and sometimes it's

00:50:08.860 --> 00:50:09.580
not visible.

00:50:10.460 --> 00:50:12.610
Whenever you have intervention from Allah,

00:50:12.870 --> 00:50:15.490
either it looks like relief came or it looks like what?

00:50:15.960 --> 00:50:16.770
Disaster came.

00:50:17.760 --> 00:50:19.100
The test of our faith

00:50:19.360 --> 00:50:20.220
first of all,

00:50:20.760 --> 00:50:24.270
we keep hoping there will be some kind of miracle like the people of the cave.

00:50:26.260 --> 00:50:28.020
And when that intervention comes,

00:50:28.030 --> 00:50:30.490
it will necessarily mean relief will come with it.

00:50:31.460 --> 00:50:33.320
And for some people Allah will give them that.

00:50:33.360 --> 00:50:35.890
But that's not the only kind of intervention from Allah.

00:50:36.660 --> 00:50:38.030
There's other kinds of intervention.

00:50:38.170 --> 00:50:40.590
Sometimes Allah intervenes and destroy somebody's garden.

00:50:40.600 --> 00:50:42.080
And was that good for him or bad for him?

00:50:43.060 --> 00:50:45.010
Even though apparently there was distress,

00:50:45.760 --> 00:50:46.780
it's actually good for him.

00:50:47.860 --> 00:50:48.860
And as a matter of fact,

00:50:48.860 --> 00:50:52.700
even though apparently the People of the Cave received relief, if they

00:50:52.700 --> 00:50:57.720
after coming back-in the worldly sense-renounce their faith, that's still distress.

00:50:57.730 --> 00:51:03.280
Which is why Allah is going to say that the only thing good is not them surviving the cave.

00:51:03.290 --> 00:51:05.380
The thing that's good is them holding onto their faith.

00:51:06.760 --> 00:51:11.490
The real good isn't worldly relief. The real good is holding on to your faith.

00:51:12.460 --> 00:51:14.570
The same thing with this guy who lost his garden.

00:51:14.570 --> 00:51:16.530
The tragedy is not that he lost his garden.

00:51:16.530 --> 00:51:18.607
Actually, the good news is at the end of it, he says:

00:51:18.632 --> 00:51:20.380
يَا لَيْتَنِي لَمْ أُشْرِكْ بِرَبِّي أَحَدًا

00:51:21.360 --> 00:51:23.160
I wish I didn't do that. He repented.

00:51:23.270 --> 00:51:24.050
There's good news.

00:51:25.760 --> 00:51:29.790
But then people's faith is tested when the trouble that

00:51:29.790 --> 00:51:32.390
comes in their life is not at
the hands of Allah visibly.

00:51:32.760 --> 00:51:34.580
it looks like it's at the hands of people.

00:51:35.960 --> 00:51:38.270
It's some Khidr who cracked the ship.

00:51:38.760 --> 00:51:39.780
Or killed a boy.

00:51:40.660 --> 00:51:42.880
Or had you build a wall without being paid for it.

00:51:44.260 --> 00:51:45.620
It's some human intervention.

00:51:46.460 --> 00:51:49.950
Allah is teaching through that lesson that even when

00:51:49.950 --> 00:51:51.850
you see that it's the act of human beings,

00:51:51.850 --> 00:51:54.190
don't forget that Allah's Will was at play.

00:51:55.560 --> 00:51:59.070
Allah would not have let this person do what they did, if it wasn't part of a plan.

00:51:59.860 --> 00:52:01.640
You may not see the benefit in that plan.

00:52:01.650 --> 00:52:03.970
How can somebody see the benefit in a child being killed?

00:52:05.150 --> 00:52:05.770
How can I?

00:52:06.450 --> 00:52:08.480
I will question it. Musa 'alaihissalam got upset.

00:52:08.950 --> 00:52:10.160
And he's Musa 'alaihissalam.

00:52:10.390 --> 00:52:12.480
And Allah told him: Go learn from this man.

00:52:13.050 --> 00:52:17.270
So it's not like he doesn't know that this is from Allah, but he lost it.

00:52:17.750 --> 00:52:18.470
How could you?

00:52:19.250 --> 00:52:21.180
And that's after he promised, "I'm going to have Sabr".

00:52:21.190 --> 00:52:23.430
So the fact that you and I will lose patience

00:52:23.430 --> 00:52:25.570
when we see things like that happen is understandable.

00:52:26.150 --> 00:52:28.270
If that can happen, even from Musa 'alaihissalam.

00:52:29.050 --> 00:52:30.570
وَكَانَ عِندَ اللَّهِ وَجِيهًا

00:52:31.150 --> 00:52:33.030
He's so noble before Allah and he can have that,

00:52:33.030 --> 00:52:35.470
then you and I having a reaction is understandable.

00:52:35.850 --> 00:52:37.260
Allah sympathizes

00:52:37.950 --> 00:52:39.480
with that sentiment, Okay?

00:52:41.050 --> 00:52:42.670
But even then he had to be taught

00:52:42.670 --> 00:52:46.570
even when bad things happen, you will always maintain a good opinion of Allah.

00:52:47.650 --> 00:52:52.600
And you will say, "Even even though this is bad, it looks bad. Apparently bad.

00:52:52.610 --> 00:52:54.405
It's apparent distress. There's something Khair

00:52:54.430 --> 00:52:56.170
in it that is beyond my comprehension."

00:52:56.850 --> 00:52:59.670
"I'm going to still give my my good good will to Allah."

00:53:00.650 --> 00:53:02.380
"My benefit of the doubt to Allah."

00:53:03.140 --> 00:53:05.230
The final case is equally dangerous.

00:53:05.360 --> 00:53:06.880
What if you have

00:53:07.250 --> 00:53:09.170
good coming from your hand?

00:53:09.850 --> 00:53:10.770
What is the tendency?

00:53:12.650 --> 00:53:14.270
When you accomplish something good,

00:53:15.450 --> 00:53:17.270
you start thinking maybe this is from

00:53:17.950 --> 00:53:18.670
my doing.

00:53:19.250 --> 00:53:21.260
Especially when relief comes to somebody.

00:53:21.950 --> 00:53:24.100
Which is why Zul Qarnain goes out of his way to say:

00:53:24.124 --> 00:53:26.124
هَذَا رَحْمَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّ

00:53:27.550 --> 00:53:28.870
هَذَا رَحْمَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّ

00:53:29.950 --> 00:53:33.570
These are --these last two are the ones where the faith is really, really tested.

00:53:34.850 --> 00:53:37.070
Where the Divine intervention is invisible.

00:53:38.250 --> 00:53:40.990
Where it's invisible it becomes extremely difficult.

00:53:41.160 --> 00:53:42.570
This is the trial of this Surah.

00:53:43.250 --> 00:53:46.420
Which is why it keeps  analyzing real reward

00:53:46.430 --> 00:53:49.180
and real punishment is not for this world.

00:53:50.150 --> 00:53:52.760
Whatever is going on with you in this world is not a punishment.

00:53:53.650 --> 00:53:58.640
That's in the Akhira. In this world, it's just trial. Apparent or not apparent.

00:53:58.650 --> 00:54:01.470
Do you understand how all those scenarios are covered in this Surah now?

00:54:01.840 --> 00:54:04.410
Just a side note about the two stories.

00:54:04.420 --> 00:54:07.260
Both of them, interestingly, have three stops each,

00:54:07.940 --> 00:54:09.926
Both of them the first stop--Musa 'alaihissalam

00:54:09.951 --> 00:54:13.250
is in a position of weakness and a position of the following.

00:54:13.940 --> 00:54:16.160
By contrast, Zul Qarnain is in a position of leading.

00:54:16.840 --> 00:54:20.350
So you've got three stops. One is a follower, the other as a leader.

00:54:20.740 --> 00:54:24.320
Musa 'alaihissalam is constantly in a position of weakness because he doesn't have the

00:54:24.320 --> 00:54:28.360
power to do stuff and Zul Qarnain is continuously in a position of power to do things.

00:54:29.540 --> 00:54:33.470
Musa 'alaihissalam sees a crime happened but you find out later on

00:54:33.470 --> 00:54:35.960
that was to prevent a wrongdoer from seizing a ship.

00:54:36.340 --> 00:54:37.560
A king from seizing a ship.

00:54:38.540 --> 00:54:41.050
By contrast, in the first stop of Zul Qarnain he says:

00:54:41.050 --> 00:54:42.560
If somebody does wrong, I'm going to punish him.

00:54:42.560 --> 00:54:43.970
And if somebody does good, I'll reward him.

00:54:44.540 --> 00:54:46.880
If you don't have the power to stop oppression,

00:54:46.880 --> 00:54:49.160
do whatever you can to at least save the oppressed.

00:54:50.840 --> 00:54:52.400
If you have the power,

00:54:52.540 --> 00:54:54.890
then punish the wrongdoer and reward the good doers.

00:54:55.640 --> 00:54:56.590
Two scenarios.

00:54:56.870 --> 00:54:57.970
The Musa scenario

00:54:58.340 --> 00:54:59.750
and the Zul Qarnain scenario.

00:55:00.340 --> 00:55:03.260
Make the best of the situation if you're in a desperate situation.

00:55:04.340 --> 00:55:06.193
The second stop, interestingly,

00:55:06.218 --> 00:55:07.470
he commits murder.

00:55:08.440 --> 00:55:10.660
He commits murder, which seems absurd.

00:55:11.140 --> 00:55:13.340
Seems unjust, and actually even

00:55:13.340 --> 00:55:15.850
what Zul Qarnain does in the second stop seems unjust. Why?

00:55:15.860 --> 00:55:18.060
He saw people that have no shade and what did he do?

00:55:19.240 --> 00:55:20.260
He just let them be.

00:55:21.240 --> 00:55:24.320
He has the power to build massive walls. He could have built something.

00:55:24.320 --> 00:55:27.060
But there are sometimes there's a situation, there's nothing you can do about it.

00:55:27.840 --> 00:55:29.910
In the case of Zul Qarnain, there's divine intervention,

00:55:29.910 --> 00:55:32.570
something terrible has happened. There's nothing you can do about that.

00:55:32.580 --> 00:55:34.330
And there's sometimes a situation in front of you,

00:55:34.330 --> 00:55:36.290
even though you might have power in other ways.

00:55:36.300 --> 00:55:38.850
You don't have the power to change it, and you have to learn to let go.

00:55:39.640 --> 00:55:42.250
That's part of your trial too. When do you accept that you don't have control?

00:55:42.940 --> 00:55:45.365
كَذَلِكَ وَقَدْ أَحَطْنَا بِمَا لَدَيْهِ خُبْرًا

00:55:45.390 --> 00:55:50.140
He left him alone and We know more about them. I'm not gonna tell you why he left them.

00:55:50.140 --> 00:55:53.050
Just know that he couldn't handle it. He had to go elsewhere.

00:55:54.140 --> 00:55:58.080
The third stop on both cases in both stories is a wall and a wall.

00:55:59.640 --> 00:56:01.460
Musa 'alaihissalam helped build a wall. For who?

00:56:02.530 --> 00:56:03.440
Couple of orphans.

00:56:04.330 --> 00:56:08.505
Zul Qarnain builds a wall to
help the people because Ya'juj and Ma'juj

00:56:08.530 --> 00:56:09.660
keep coming and attacking.

00:56:10.130 --> 00:56:13.250
One wall is designed to fall apart

00:56:13.930 --> 00:56:15.040
as a mercy from Allah.

00:56:16.330 --> 00:56:18.960
Because eventually, what will they do? The youth?

00:56:19.530 --> 00:56:22.650
When they get old enough, they'll open the wall and they'll take the treasure out.

00:56:23.230 --> 00:56:27.985
The other wall is designed- reinforcement, copper, iron. What's the point?

00:56:28.010 --> 00:56:30.418
فَمَا اسْطَاعُوا أَن يَظْهَرُوهُ وَمَا اسْتَطَاعُوا لَهُ نَقْبًا

00:56:30.480 --> 00:56:34.450
It's by design made so that it never, ever, ever falls.

00:56:34.450 --> 00:56:38.100
And even though it's designed to never, ever, ever, fall Zul Qrnain says:

00:56:38.125 --> 00:56:39.250
Yeah, this is not forever.

00:56:40.030 --> 00:56:44.025
فَإِذَا جَاءَ وَعْدُ رَبِّي جَعَلَهُ دَكَّاء وَكَانَ وَعْدُ رَبِّي حَقًّا

00:56:44.050 --> 00:56:44.950
It's gonna fall.

00:56:45.730 --> 00:56:48.670
When the first wall falls, it'll be an apparent good.

00:56:49.830 --> 00:56:52.460
And when then second wall falls, it'll be an apparent what?

00:56:52.930 --> 00:56:53.550
Bad.

00:56:54.330 --> 00:56:57.240
Both have built a wall, but opposite things are going to happen.

00:56:57.830 --> 00:56:58.250
Okay?

00:56:58.830 --> 00:57:02.040
And yet both of their falling is part of the plan of Allah.

00:57:03.430 --> 00:57:04.840
وَعْدُ رَبِّي
وَعْدُ رَبِّي

00:57:05.830 --> 00:57:09.460
When Khidr describes why he built the wall? You know what he said?

00:57:10.830 --> 00:57:14.660
He said
فَأَرَادَ رَبُّكَ أَنْ يَبْلُغَا أَشُدَّهُمَا

00:57:15.530 --> 00:57:18.640
Your master intended that they should both reach mature age

00:57:19.010 --> 00:57:22.340
وَيَسْتَخْرِجَا كَنزَهُمَا
They should take out the treasure that belongs to them.

00:57:23.030 --> 00:57:24.550
رَحْمَةً مِّن رَّبِّكَ

00:57:25.930 --> 00:57:29.540
All of that is there for what? As a mercy from your Master.

00:57:29.680 --> 00:57:33.279
When Zul Qarnain finishes building his wall, what does he say?

00:57:33.304 --> 00:57:35.570
هَذَا رَحْمَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّ

00:57:36.647 --> 00:57:38.340
فَإِذَا جَاءَ وَعْدُ
This is a mercy.

00:57:39.030 --> 00:57:42.500
In one case, the time when the wall will break will be Rahma.

00:57:42.510 --> 00:57:45.660
And the other case, as long as the wall is standing, is a Rahma.

00:57:47.330 --> 00:57:48.550
But none of these are permanent

00:57:48.550 --> 00:57:52.449
because this life isn't permanent
وَإِنَّا لَجَاعِلُونَ مَا عَلَيْهَا صَعِيدًا جُرُزًا

00:57:52.520 --> 00:57:56.660
Good is not forever, bad is not forever. Both are highlighted.

00:57:56.670 --> 00:57:58.430
It's a remarkable picture,

00:57:58.430 --> 00:58:02.660
one item at a time of all the scenarios that you and I will experience in this life.

00:58:03.030 --> 00:58:06.280
Of Allah's intervention, of good situations and of bad situations.

00:58:06.290 --> 00:58:09.500
And that's a structural overview of Surat al-Kahf.

00:58:09.510 --> 00:58:10.460
Okay, so I've

00:58:10.830 --> 00:58:12.540
fried your brains enough for one day, I think.

00:58:13.030 --> 00:58:16.530
Inshallahu Ta'ala. Even if I told you more, you wouldn't

00:58:16.540 --> 00:58:17.740
you wouldn't know what to do with it.

00:58:18.230 --> 00:58:20.505
Because your minds are somewhere else now. So Inshallah Ta'ala

00:58:20.530 --> 00:58:23.370
I'll conclude with that, and we will pick up our study tomorrow.

00:58:23.370 --> 00:58:25.890
Maybe we'll do one more linear study and then go

00:58:25.890 --> 00:58:28.130
to anchors and then go to the structural study of Surahs.

00:58:29.900 --> 00:58:32.007
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُم وَرَحْمَةُ اللهِ وَ بَرَكَاتُهُ